[?2004l0 p 'We have 20 vowel sounds, and 24 consonant sounds.We have 20 vowel sounds, and 24 consonant sounds.We have 20 vowel sounds, and 24 consonant sounds.-88899-25399Graphemes = Sound Letter Patterns Graphemes = Sound Letter Patterns Graphemes = Sound Letter Patterns English can be thought of as an alphabetic language consisting of 44 speech sounds (phonemes) which map onto letter patterns (graphemes).English can be thought of as an alphabetic language consisting of 44 speech sounds (phonemes) which map onto letter patterns (graphemes).English can be thought of as an alphabetic language consisting of 44 speech sounds (phonemes) which map onto letter patterns (graphemes).-88899-25399'
1 p 'In English we use graphemes to represent these various sounds (phonemes). In English we use graphemes to represent these various sounds (phonemes). In English we use graphemes to represent these various sounds (phonemes). '
2 p 'Graphemes can be a single letter (graph), or a combination of two (digraph), three (trigraph), or four letters (quadgraph). Graphemes can be a single letter (graph), or a combination of two (digraph), three (trigraph), or four letters (quadgraph). Graphemes can be a single letter (graph), or a combination of two (digraph), three (trigraph), or four letters (quadgraph). '
